return array(
	'about_0_b' => 'Ines Kovač founded the practice in 2011 in Elsmere Quay. Five people work from the office at 3 Ropewalk Yard. There is one van, one ladder and one pole camera, and the week\'s visits are booked by the request desk rather than by a call centre. Tomasz Wren, Adaeze Nwosu, Henrik Saari and Ines survey about twelve buildings a week.',
	'about_0_c' => 'Lucía Pardo books every visit and writes the reply within one working day, with a fixed price and a slot. We spend about 90 minutes on a flat or small house and up to about four hours on a small commercial building, then write the report in plain words. The work stops at the report and the 30-minute call. The repair, if there is one, stays with the people who own that decision.',
	'about_0_h' => 'The practice',
	'about_1_b' => 'The day starts at 07:45, when the van is loaded: ladder, pole camera, damp meter and torch. The first visit is at 08:30. At 12:30 the photographs are uploaded from the van, so the morning visit is already in the file before the afternoon begins. At 14:00 there is a second visit, or writing at the office. At 17:00 Lucía confirms tomorrow\'s slots and replies to the day\'s requests.',
	'about_1_c' => 'Site visits run Monday to Saturday, 08:00–17:00, Saturday by arrangement. The request desk is Monday to Friday, 08:30–17:30. Every request that arrives in those desk hours is answered within one working day. The rhythm is the same in winter. If frost or rain keeps us off a roof, the report says what the pole camera could not see.',
	'about_1_h' => 'A day',
	'about_2_b' => 'Ines Kovač is the founder and lead surveyor. She takes commercial buildings and older houses, and she is the person the practice was built around in 2011. Tomasz Wren surveys houses. He is the surveyor on the ladder in front of a brick terrace, photographing a lintel or a sill with a clipboard under one arm. Adaeze Nwosu works on damp and interiors.',
	'about_2_c' => 'She reads the meter at the skirting, checks the air bricks and writes the difference between condensation and rising damp in plain words. Henrik Saari surveys small commercial buildings: the shopfront, the flat roof, the fire escape and the separation between a shop and a flat. Lucía Pardo runs the request desk. She books every visit and writes the reply within one working day. Five people, named on the report, not a rotating roster.',
	'about_2_h' => 'Who comes to the house',
	'about_3_b' => 'We do not sell or arrange repairs. The rough cost range in the priorities is there so you can talk to the seller or to a contractor you choose. It is not a quotation from us, and we do not introduce a builder. We do not work for the seller or the agent. The instruction comes from the buyer, and the report goes to the named client.',
	'about_3_c' => 'A survey is not a valuation. We do not tell you what the building is worth, and we do not dress a condition report up as a price. We also do not say the report has found every defect. It records what could be seen on the day, and it says when something could not be seen.',
	'about_3_h' => 'What we are not',
	'about_4_b' => 'The office is at 3 Ropewalk Yard, Elsmere Quay. Email hello@noki-surveyors.example and phone +00 31 555 0148 reach the request desk. Desk hours are Monday to Friday, 08:30–17:30. Site visits are Monday to Saturday, 08:00–17:00, and Saturday is by arrangement.',
	'about_4_c' => 'The survey area is within 40 km of Elsmere Quay, and travel inside that distance is included in the published prices. If you would rather write than call, the request form asks for the address, the type of building and the date you need the report by. Lucía replies within one working day with a fixed price and a visit slot.',
