	'list_l' => 'Notes',
	'list_p' => 'Notes are short pieces from the surveyors on findings and on the way a building reads in the field. They sit beside the case notes, and they use the same buildings and the same limits.',
	'newsletter_0_b' => 'The survey diary fills up with house visits and commercial half-days, Monday to Saturday. When a slot opens, a slot alert is the note that says so. It is for people who already know they want a survey and are waiting for a day, not for a general mailing about the practice.',
	'newsletter_0_c' => 'Lucía Pardo books every visit. An alert does not reserve a building for you. It tells you there is room to ask. You still send the address, the type of building and the date you need the report by, and you still receive a fixed price within one working day.',
	'newsletter_0_h' => 'Get an email when visit slots open',
	'newsletter_1_b' => 'You get at most two emails a month. They cover only slot openings and winter notes. A winter note is the practical kind: in frost or rain we check roofs from the ground and with a pole camera, and the report says plainly what could not be seen.',
	'newsletter_1_c' => 'We do not attach offers, and we do not write about repairs we could arrange, because we do not sell or arrange repairs. There is no weekly letter and no digest of the case notes. If a month has nothing to say about slots or about winter access, you should not expect mail for the sake of it. Two in a month is the ceiling, not a target.',
	'newsletter_1_h' => 'What you get',
	'newsletter_2_b' => 'The form asks for your email address. The button says Get slot alerts. Sending it opens your email app with your address filled in. The notice beside the form says: this opens your email app with your address filled in. Send it to get slot alerts; you are not on the list until we reply.',
	'newsletter_2_c' => 'The subject line on that message is Slot alerts: Noki Surveyors. We reply from hello@noki-surveyors.example. Until that reply, you are not signed up, and you should not expect the alerts. We would rather the step be visible than imply that a typed address is already a list.',
	'newsletter_2_h' => 'How the signup works',
	'newsletter_3_b' => 'A slot alert is the wrong tool if you already have an address and a date. Request the survey directly and Lucía replies within one working day with a fixed price and a visit slot. Desk hours are Monday to Friday, 08:30–17:30.',
	'newsletter_3_c' => 'The phone is +00 31 555 0148 and the email is hello@noki-surveyors.example. Prices include VAT and travel within 40 km of Elsmere Quay. You pay after the report is sent, within 14 days. The alert list does not change those terms, and joining it does not book a visit.',
	'newsletter_3_h' => 'If you need a survey now',
	'newsletter_i' => 'Slot alerts are a short email when visit slots open. They are sent from hello@noki-surveyors.example, and they are separate from the notes archive.',
	'newsletter_l' => 'Slot alerts',
	'newsletter_t' => 'Slot alerts',
	'no_posts' => 'Nothing here yet.',
	'notice_line' => 'In frost or rain we check roofs from the ground and with a pole camera; the report says plainly what could not be seen.',
	'notice_s' => 'Notice',
	'notice_t' => 'Winter visits',
	'pa_1' => 'a flat',
	'pa_2' => 'a house',
	'pa_3' => 'a large house',
