	'pb_1' => 'cracks',
	'pb_2' => 'damp',
	'pb_3' => 'the roof',
	'ppl_h' => 'Who comes to the house',
	'ppl_l' => 'People',
	'ppl_p' => 'Ines Kovač founded Noki Surveyors in 2011 in Elsmere Quay. Five people work from 3 Ropewalk Yard, with one van, one ladder and one pole camera. The survey area is within 40 km of Elsmere Quay, and about twelve buildings are surveyed in a week.',
	'pr1_a' => 'Flat or small house',
	'pr1_b' => 'Up to 90 m², full condition report',
	'pr1_c' => 'about 90 min',
	'pr1_d' => 'EUR 480',
	'pr2_a' => 'House',
	'pr2_b' => '90–180 m², full condition report',
	'pr2_c' => '2–3 h',
	'pr2_d' => 'EUR 640',
	'pr3_a' => 'Large house',
	'pr3_b' => 'Over 180 m² or with outbuildings',
	'pr3_c' => '3–4 h',
	'pr3_d' => 'EUR 820',
	'pr4_a' => 'Small commercial building',
	'pr4_b' => 'Shop, office or workshop up to 400 m², including a flat above',
	'pr4_c' => 'about 4 h',
	'pr4_d' => 'EUR 1,150',
	'pr5_a' => 'Single-defect inspection',
	'pr5_b' => 'One crack, damp patch or leak, short letter',
	'pr5_c' => 'about 45 min',
	'pr5_d' => 'EUR 290',
	'pr6_a' => 'Re-visit after repairs',
	'pr6_b' => 'Checks the agreed repair, short letter',
	'pr6_c' => 'about 45 min',
	'pr6_d' => 'EUR 160',
	'pr_h' => 'Prices',
	'pr_l' => 'Prices',
	'pr_note' => 'Prices include VAT and travel within 40 km of Elsmere Quay. Every full report includes a 30-minute call. You pay after the report is sent, within 14 days.',
	'pri_1_p' => 'Deal with it before you commit, or as soon as the building is yours.',
	'pri_1_t' => 'Now',
	'pri_2_p' => 'Work that can wait, and should not be forgotten.',
	'pri_2_t' => 'Within two years',
	'pri_3_p' => 'A crack, a stain or a slope we record so you can look again later.',
	'pri_3_t' => 'Keep an eye on',
	'pri_t' => 'Priorities, in three columns',
	'prices_0_b' => 'In frost or rain we check roofs from the ground and with a pole camera; the report says plainly what could not be seen. Ladders still go to about 3 m where that is safe, and single-storey roofs can be seen from a ladder. We never walk on roofs. A winter visit is the same service as any other: a fixed price, agreed before we come, and a report that separates what was seen from what the weather or the height kept hidden. If you need the report by a set date, say so when you request the survey. Lucía replies within one working day with the price and the slot.',
	'prices_1_b' => 'Flat or small house: up to 90 m², full condition report, about 90 minutes on site, EUR 480. House: 90–180 m², full condition report, 2 to 3 hours, EUR 640. Large house: over 180 m² or with outbuildings, 3 to 4 hours, EUR 820. Small commercial building: shop, office or workshop up to 400 m², including a flat above, about 4 hours, EUR 1,150.',
	'prices_1_c' => 'Single-defect inspection: one crack, damp patch or leak, short letter, about 45 minutes, EUR 290. Re-visit after repairs: checks the agreed repair, short letter, about 45 minutes, EUR 160. Prices include VAT and travel within 40 km of Elsmere Quay. Every full report includes a 30-minute call. You pay after the report is sent, within 14 days.',
	'prices_1_h' => 'The six surveys',
	'prices_2_b' => 'Flat or small house, about 90 minutes. House of 90–180 m², 2 to 3 hours. Large house, 3 to 4 hours. Small commercial building, about 4 hours, half a day. Single-defect inspection or re-visit, about 45 minutes. The hero line we use for the whole range is 90 minutes to 4 hours on site. Someone needs to let us in.',
	'prices_2_c' => 'You do not have to stay. You are welcome to join for the last 20 minutes. Site visits run Monday to Saturday, 08:00–17:00, Saturday by arrangement. The full report follows within 5 working days of the visit. A single-defect letter or a re-visit letter follows within 2 working days. A 30-minute call follows the report or the letter.',
	'prices_2_h' => 'How long a visit takes',
	'prices_3_b' => 'We survey within 40 km of Elsmere Quay. Travel inside that distance is included in the price, along with VAT. The office is at 3 Ropewalk Yard, Elsmere Quay. If the building is outside the 40 km, we say so when Lucía replies, rather than stretching the published price to cover it.',
	'prices_3_c' => 'The request needs the address so we can see that the visit sits inside the area before we confirm the slot. The same boundary applies to a full condition report, a single-defect inspection and a re-visit after repairs.',
	'prices_3_h' => 'Travel and the working area',
	'prices_4_b' => 'You pay after the report is sent, within 14 days. The price Lucía confirms is fixed, and it is agreed before the visit. There is no separate travel bill inside 40 km of Elsmere Quay, and VAT is already in the figure.',
	'prices_4_c' => 'A full report is due within 5 working days of the visit and includes the 30-minute call. Single-defect and re-visit letters are due within 2 working days. Cancellation is free until 24 hours before the visit. The request desk is open Monday to Friday, 08:30–17:30, and every request is answered within one working day.',
	'prices_4_h' => 'How payment works',
	'prices_5_b' => 'A survey is a visual, non-invasive look at the building. It does not include testing the electrics, the heating or the drains. We do not lift fixed floors. We may turn a carpet corner where we are allowed. We never walk on roofs. Ladders go to about 3 m, single-storey roofs are seen from a ladder, and otherwise we use a pole camera and binoculars.',
	'prices_5_c' => 'We do not sell or arrange repairs. We do not work for the seller or the agent. A survey is not a valuation. If something serious needs a structural engineer or another specialist, we say so on the call and name the kind of person to ask. You instruct them yourself.',
	'prices_5_h' => 'What a survey does not include',
	'prices_i' => 'Every request is answered within one working day with a fixed price and a visit slot. The six prices below are in EUR, include VAT, and are the same ones we confirm before anyone comes to site.',
	'prices_l' => 'Visits & prices',
	'prices_t' => 'Visits & prices',
	'privacy_0_b' => 'Noki Surveyors is the building surveying practice founded in 2011 by Ines Kovač. The request desk is run by Lucía Pardo. You can reach us at hello@noki-surveyors.example or on +00 31 555 0148, Monday to Friday, 08:30–17:30. We survey within 40 km of Elsmere Quay.',
	'privacy_0_c' => 'This note describes what you give us when you request a survey, when you write to the desk, and when you ask for slot alerts. It stays with this practice. We do not work for the seller or the agent, and we do not pass your request to them.',
	'privacy_0_h' => 'Who we are',
	'privacy_1_b' => 'The request form collects your name, email and phone, the property address, the building type, the approximate age of the building, the date you need the report by, who lets us in, your main concern and your message. The building types match the price list, from a flat or small house up to 90 m² through to a re-visit. The age bands are before 1919, 1919–1945, 1945–1980, after 1980, or don\'t know.',
	'privacy_1_c' => 'Who lets us in is the agent, the seller, the tenant or you. The concern is cracks, damp, the roof or other. You tick a consent line: I agree that Noki Surveyors may reply about this request. We use those fields to answer within one working day with a fixed price and a visit slot, and then to carry out the survey.',
	'privacy_1_h' => 'The survey request',
	'privacy_2_b' => 'The contact form collects your name, your email, your message and your consent. We use it to reply. The confirmation, when the message has been sent through the form, is: Thank you. Lucía will reply within one working day. Slot alerts collect an email address. We use it only to send slot openings and winter notes, at most two emails a month.',
	'privacy_2_c' => 'You are not on the list until we reply. The signup message is addressed to hello@noki-surveyors.example with the subject Slot alerts: Noki Surveyors. If the form opens your email app, the alert subscription is not complete until that reply exists. We do not add you on the strength of a typed address alone.',
	'privacy_2_h' => 'Contact messages and slot alerts',
	'privacy_3_b' => 'The report is for the named client only. Only you see it, unless you share it. We do not send it to the seller or the agent. We do not work for them. Photographs in the report are of the building we were asked to survey. The 30-minute call is with you.',
	'privacy_3_c' => 'A case note on this site uses the client\'s name only where that person is Ruth Bell, Sana Iqbal or Dev Anand, in the stories already agreed for publication. Other reports stay off the site. We do not sell the enquiry list, and we do not sell or arrange repairs from the details you gave us.',
	'privacy_3_h' => 'The report and who sees it',
	'privacy_4_b' => 'If you want to know what we hold from a request, or if you want slot alerts to stop, email hello@noki-surveyors.example or call +00 31 555 0148 during desk hours, Monday to Friday, 08:30–17:30. Lucía handles the desk. Say the address of the property, or the email you used, so we can find the right request.',
	'privacy_4_c' => 'A request for a survey still needs the address, the type of building and the date you need the report by. Taking your name off the slot alerts does not cancel a visit that is already booked. Cancellation of a visit is free until 24 hours before the visit, which is set out in the terms.',
	'privacy_4_h' => 'Writing to us about your details',
	'privacy_i' => 'Noki Surveyors holds the details you send so we can reply, book a visit and write the report for you. The office is at 3 Ropewalk Yard, Elsmere Quay.',
	'privacy_l' => 'Privacy',
	'privacy_t' => 'Privacy',
	'pt_h1' => 'Survey',
	'pt_h2' => 'What it covers',
	'pt_h3' => 'On site',
	'pt_h4' => 'Price',
	'q1_p' => 'We measure the crack width, look at which way it steps and whether the lintel above it has dropped. The report says whether the movement looks old and quiet or should be repaired before you commit, and names the kind of specialist to ask if it needs one.',
	'q1_t' => 'Cracks',
	'q2_p' => 'We take readings at the skirting, check air bricks and look for condensation against a cold external wall. A tide mark is not always rising damp. The report says what the readings showed and what a small fix would involve, with a photograph.',
	'q2_t' => 'Damp',
	'q3_m' => 'Pole camera, from the pavement',
	'q3_p' => 'We look at coverings, flashings, gutters and downpipes from a ladder to about 3 m or with a pole camera. We do not walk on roofs. The report says what could be seen, including slipped slates or ponding, and what the weather stopped us seeing.',
	'q3_t' => 'The roof',
	'q_h' => 'Questions',
	'q_l' => 'Questions',
	'q_more' => 'Inside the report →',
	'qa1_a' => 'Someone needs to let us in. You do not have to stay for the whole visit. You are welcome to join for the last 20 minutes, when the surveyor can walk you through what they have seen.',
	'qa1_q' => 'Do I need to be there?',
	'qa2_a' => 'We use ladders to about 3 m and we look at single-storey roofs from those ladders. Above that we use a pole camera and binoculars. We never walk on roofs. If frost or rain hides something, the report says plainly what could not be seen.',
	'qa2_q' => 'Do you go on the roof?',
	'qa3_a' => 'We do not lift fixed floors. Where we are allowed, we lift carpet corners to see the boards and the skirting. Furniture stays where it is.',
	'qa3_q' => 'Do you lift floors or move furniture?',
	'qa4_a' => 'No. A survey is a condition report. It is not a valuation, and it does not tell you what the building is worth.',
	'qa4_q' => 'Is this a valuation?',
	'qa5_a' => 'Only you, unless you share it. The report is for the named client. We do not work for the seller or the agent, and we do not send them a copy unless you ask us to.',
	'qa5_q' => 'Who sees the report?',
	'qa6_a' => 'We say so on the 30-minute call and we name the kind of specialist to ask, such as a structural engineer. We do not sell or arrange the repair.',
	'qa6_q' => 'What if you find something serious?',
	'rep_btn' => 'See the report page',
	'rep_h' => 'Inside the report',
	'rep_l' => 'The report',
	'rep_ledger_h' => 'Eight sections, one report',
	'rep_ledger_l' => 'The ledger',
	'rep_note' => 'Every finding has a photograph and a plain-words sentence. The full report is sent within 5 working days of the visit, then we talk it through on a 30-minute call. Single-defect and re-visit letters take 2 working days.',
	'report_0_b' => 'We write the way we would explain the house to you on the pavement. Each finding is one photograph and one sentence in plain words: what we saw, where it is, and why it matters before you sign. The report uses eight numbered sections, and the last of them sorts the findings into three columns: now, within two years, and keep an eye on.',
	'report_0_c' => 'Each item in those columns carries a rough cost range, so you can talk to the seller with something concrete in front of you. The range is a scale for that conversation. We do not sell or arrange repairs. The report is prepared for the named client. A survey is not a valuation. Where a floor, a roof or a service could not be seen, the sentence says that plainly.',
	'report_0_h' => 'How we write',
	'report_1_b' => 'This section covers cracks, lintels, floors and the chimney. We look at whether a crack is only in the plaster or whether it steps through the brick, and which way it runs. On a cracked brick lintel over a bay we note whether the lintel has dropped and whether the masonry above is opening.',
	'report_1_c' => 'Floors are read for slope and for how they feel underfoot. The chimney is checked where we can see it, inside and out, for cracked pots, open joints and movement where it meets the roof. We do not open up the structure. If a finding needs a structural engineer, we say so on the 30-minute call and name that kind of specialist.',
	'report_1_h' => 'Structure and movement',
	'report_2_b' => 'This section covers roof coverings, flashings, gutters and downpipes. We look at slipped or cracked slates, open joints at a valley, and felt flat roofs that hold water. Flashings are checked where the roof meets a wall or a chimney. Gutters and downpipes are read for leaks, blockages and stains on the wall beneath them.',
	'report_2_c' => 'In frost or rain we check roofs from the ground and with a pole camera, and the report says plainly what could not be seen. Ladders go to about 3 m, and we look at single-storey roofs from a ladder. Otherwise we use the pole camera and binoculars. We never walk on roofs.',
	'report_2_h' => 'Roof and rainwater',
	'report_3_b' => 'This section records damp readings, air bricks and signs of condensation. We hold a damp meter against walls and skirtings where we can reach them, and we write the readings into the report. A high reading is not a diagnosis on its own. We look for a tide mark above the skirting, a blocked air brick, and cold surfaces where moisture can settle.',
	'report_3_c' => 'A damp patch at the skirting can be condensation rather than rising damp, and the report says which one the readings and the ventilation support. We do not lift fixed floors. Where a carpet corner can be turned, we look at the boards and the skirting behind it.',
	'report_3_h' => 'Damp and ventilation',
	'report_4_b' => 'This section covers outside walls, windows and doors. We look at brick and render for cracks, open joints and patches of repair. Window sills are checked for cracks, and frames for rot and for sashes that do not close. Doors are noted where they bind, where the threshold lets water in, or where the frame has moved with the wall.',
	'report_4_c' => 'A cracked sill or a lintel over a window is written with a photograph and one plain sentence, so you can see the same thing we saw. The note stays with the condition of the fabric. A survey is not a valuation of the house, and it does not price the windows as a quote for replacement. We do not sell or arrange repairs.',
	'report_4_h' => 'Walls, windows and doors',
	'report_5_b' => 'Services we can see covers visible electrics, heating and drainage covers. The inspection is visual only. It is not a test. We note cables, fittings and the heater where they are in sight, and we look at drainage covers we can open. If a cover stays shut, or a fitting is hidden, the report says what could not be seen.',
	'report_5_c' => 'When a finding needs an electrician, a heating engineer or someone who tests drains, we name that kind of specialist on the 30-minute call. You arrange any further test yourself. We do not sell or arrange the work, and looking at a service does not amount to saying it is safe or complete.',
	'report_5_h' => 'Services we can see',
	'report_6_b' => 'Inside, we look at ceilings, stairs and fire escape routes. Ceilings are checked for cracks and stains, including stains that line up with a leak above. Stairs are walked. We note loose treads, a missing handrail and any slope that is hard to ignore. In a house, the escape route is the stair and the hall to the outside door.',
	'report_6_c' => 'In a shop with a flat above, we look at the separation between the shop and the flat and whether the escape route from the flat is clear. We write what we could see on the day, with a photograph where the ceiling or the route needs one. We do not design a fire strategy, and we do not sell or arrange repairs.',
	'report_6_h' => 'Inside',
	'report_7_b' => 'Outside, we look at boundaries, paths, outbuildings and trees near walls. Boundaries are walls, fences and the ground along them: we note cracks, leans and places where the ground is higher on one side. Paths are checked where water sits against the house. Outbuildings are included when they belong with a large house, and they are part of why that visit runs to three or four hours.',
	'report_7_c' => 'A tree close to a wall is recorded where the canopy, the roots or a stain meet the building. We do not say who owns a boundary. The note is there so you can raise a tree or a leaning wall before you sign.',
	'report_7_h' => 'Outside',
	'report_8_b' => 'The last section sorts findings into three columns: now, within two years, and keep an eye on. Now means something to deal with before you commit, or as soon as the building is yours, such as a lintel to replace before winter or a flat roof that is holding water. Within two years means work that can wait and should not be forgotten.',
	'report_8_c' => 'Keep an eye on means a crack, a stain or a slope we record so you can look again later. Each item has a rough cost range for a conversation with the seller. We do not sell or arrange the repairs. The 30-minute call after the report walks through these three columns with you.',
	'report_8_h' => 'Priorities',
	'report_9_b' => 'Recent reports have included slipped slates at a valley on a 1930s semi, a tide mark above the skirting in a ground-floor flat, a cracked lintel over a bay window on a 1920s terrace, an upstairs floor falling 18 mm towards the front wall, and ponding on a felt flat roof behind a shop with a flat above.',
	'report_9_c' => 'On the lintel, the lintel had dropped about 4 mm, and we wrote: replace before winter, ask the seller. Each photograph sits with one plain sentence. The same five subjects are the ones we return to when a buyer asks what a visit actually finds. They are condition, written down, before anyone signs.',
	'report_9_h' => 'Photographs from recent reports',
	'report_i' => 'A Noki Surveyors report is a written record of what we could see on the day, in plain words, with a photograph for every finding. It arrives within five working days of the visit, and we follow it with a 30-minute call.',
	'report_l' => 'The report',
	'report_t' => 'The report',
	'request_0_b' => 'Send the request with three things we cannot price without: the address of the building, the type of building, and the date you need the report by. The address lets us see that the visit sits within 40 km of Elsmere Quay. The type of building points to one of the six published prices, so the figure Lucía confirms is the list price, not a fresh negotiation.',
	'request_0_c' => 'The date keeps the five working days, or the two working days on a letter, honest. You can add the concern that prompted the request, such as cracks, damp or the roof. Someone will need to let us in on the day. You are welcome for the last 20 minutes, and you do not have to stay for the rest.',
	'request_0_h' => 'What to tell us',
	'request_1_b' => 'The question we ask ourselves on every instruction is simple: what should the report tell you? If you are buying a flat, a house, a large house, or a shop or office, say which, and say whether you want to know about cracks, damp or the roof. A flat points to the survey up to 90 m².',
	'request_1_c' => 'A house points to 90–180 m². A large house is over 180 m² or has outbuildings. A shop or office is the small commercial visit. Cracks are read in the structure section, damp in the ventilation section, and the roof in the roof and rainwater section. The form is only the request. The report is the long answer, after the visit.',
	'request_1_h' => 'I am buying',
	'request_2_b' => 'Flat or small house, up to 90 m², about 90 minutes, EUR 480. House, 90–180 m², 2 to 3 hours, EUR 640. Large house, over 180 m² or with outbuildings, 3 to 4 hours, EUR 820. Small commercial building, up to 400 m² including a flat above, about 4 hours, EUR 1,150. Single-defect inspection, about 45 minutes, EUR 290.',
	'request_2_c' => 'Re-visit after repairs, about 45 minutes, EUR 160. Prices include VAT and travel within 40 km of Elsmere Quay. Every full report includes a 30-minute call. You pay after the report is sent, within 14 days. Full reports are sent within five working days. Single-defect and re-visit letters are sent within two working days.',
	'request_2_h' => 'Prices, in short',
	'request_3_b' => '01 Send the request form, or an email, with the address, the type of building and the date you need the report by. 02 Within one working day Lucía replies with a fixed price and a visit slot. 03 The surveyor visits; someone lets us in, and you are welcome to join for the last 20 minutes.',
	'request_3_c' => '04 The report arrives within five working days, followed by a 30-minute call. A single-defect or re-visit letter arrives within two working days, and the call still follows. Site visits run Monday to Saturday, 08:00–17:00, Saturday by arrangement. The request desk is Monday to Friday, 08:30–17:30.',
	'request_3_h' => 'What happens next',
	'request_4_b' => 'The form asks for your name, email and phone, the property address, and the building type: flat or small house up to 90 m², house 90–180 m², large house, small commercial, single defect, or re-visit. It asks the approximate age: before 1919, 1919–1945, 1945–1980, after 1980, or don\'t know.',
	'request_4_c' => 'It asks the date you need the report by, who lets us in (agent, seller, tenant or you), and the main concern: cracks, damp, roof or other. There is room for a message. The consent line reads: I agree that Noki Surveyors may reply about this request. The button says Send request. We use those answers to price the visit and to book it. We do not work for the seller or the agent.',
	'request_4_h' => 'The request form',
	'request_5_b' => 'If the form is not available, email hello@noki-surveyors.example with the subject Survey request. The button we leave in its place says Email your survey request. Tell us the address, the type of building and the date you need the report by. We reply within one working day.',
	'request_5_c' => 'The desk hours are Monday to Friday, 08:30–17:30. A phone call on +00 31 555 0148 reaches the same desk. Whichever way the request arrives, Lucía is the person who writes back, with a fixed price and a visit slot, before a surveyor is sent out.',
	'request_5_h' => 'Email your survey request',
	'request_email_button' => 'Email your survey request',
	'request_fallback_note' => 'Tell us the address, the type of building and the date you need the report by. We reply within one working day.',
	'request_i' => 'Tell us the address, the type of building and the date you need the report by. Lucía Pardo replies within one working day with a fixed price and a visit slot.',
	'request_l' => 'Request',
	'request_mail_subject' => 'Survey request',
	'request_t' => 'Request a survey',
	'rq_a' => 'Survey area',
	'rq_av' => 'Within 40 km of Elsmere Quay',
	'rq_d' => 'Request desk',
	'rq_dv' => 'Mon–Fri 08:30–17:30',
	'rq_e' => 'Email',
	'rq_h' => 'Request a survey',
	'rq_o' => 'Office',
	'rq_ov' => '3 Ropewalk Yard, Elsmere Quay',
	'rq_p' => 'Tell us the address, the type of building and the date you need the report by. Lucía replies within one working day with a fixed price and a visit slot.',
	'rq_t' => 'Phone',
	'rq_v' => 'Site visits',
	'rq_vv' => 'Mon–Sat 08:00–17:00, Saturday by arrangement',
	's_1' => 'I am buying',
	's_2' => 'and I want to know about',
	's_a' => 'a house',
	's_b' => 'cracks',
	'st1_l' => 'Commercial buildings and older houses.',
	'st1_n' => 'Ines Kovač',
	'st1_r' => 'Founder, lead surveyor',
	'st2_l' => 'The surveyor on the ladder, photographing lintels and roofs.',
	'st2_n' => 'Tomasz Wren',
	'st2_r' => 'House surveys',
	'st3_l' => 'Readings, air bricks and the rooms inside.',
	'st3_n' => 'Adaeze Nwosu',
	'st3_r' => 'Damp and interiors',
	'st4_l' => 'Shops, offices and workshops up to 400 m².',
	'st4_n' => 'Henrik Saari',
	'st4_r' => 'Small commercial',
	'st5_l' => 'Books every visit and replies within one working day.',
	'st5_n' => 'Lucía Pardo',
	'st5_r' => 'Request desk',
	'terms_0_b' => 'A survey records the condition of a house or a small commercial building as we could see it on the day of the visit. We look at structure and movement, roof and rainwater, damp and ventilation, walls, windows and doors, services we can see, the inside, and the outside. Every finding has a photograph and a plain-words sentence.',
	'terms_0_c' => 'Priorities are set out in three columns: now, within two years, and keep an eye on, each with a rough cost range. The range is for your conversation with the seller or with a contractor you choose. We do not sell or arrange repairs. A survey is not a valuation. We do not state what the building is worth.',
	'terms_0_h' => 'The scope of a survey',
	'terms_1_b' => 'The inspection does not include a test of the electrics, the heating or the drains. Services are recorded only where they are visible. We do not lift fixed floors. We turn a carpet corner only where we are allowed, and we say if we could not. We never walk on roofs. Ladders are used to about 3 m, and single-storey roofs may be seen from a ladder.',
	'terms_1_c' => 'Otherwise we use a pole camera and binoculars. In frost or rain we check roofs from the ground and with a pole camera, and the report says plainly what could not be seen. Hidden structure stays hidden. We do not open walls, and we do not claim to have listed every defect in the building.',
	'terms_1_h' => 'What is outside the survey',
	'terms_2_b' => 'Flat or small house, up to 90 m², about 90 minutes, EUR 480. House, 90–180 m², 2 to 3 hours, EUR 640. Large house, over 180 m² or with outbuildings, 3 to 4 hours, EUR 820. Small commercial building, up to 400 m² including a flat above, about 4 hours, EUR 1,150. Single-defect inspection, about 45 minutes, EUR 290. Re-visit after repairs, about 45 minutes, EUR 160.',
	'terms_2_c' => 'Prices include VAT and travel within 40 km of Elsmere Quay. Every full report includes a 30-minute call. You pay after the report is sent, within 14 days. The full report is sent within five working days of the visit. Single-defect and re-visit letters are sent within two working days. Lucía confirms the price and the slot within one working day of the request.',
	'terms_2_h' => 'Time, price and the call',
	'terms_3_b' => 'The price is fixed before the visit. You pay after the report, or the short letter, is sent, and payment is due within 14 days. There is no added travel charge inside 40 km of Elsmere Quay. VAT is included in the published figure. Cancellation is free until 24 hours before the visit.',
	'terms_3_c' => 'After that point the slot has been held and the day arranged, so write to the desk as soon as the timing changes. The request desk is Monday to Friday, 08:30–17:30, at hello@noki-surveyors.example and on +00 31 555 0148. Site visits run Monday to Saturday, 08:00–17:00, Saturday by arrangement. Someone needs to let the surveyor in. You are welcome for the last 20 minutes.',
	'terms_3_h' => 'Payment and cancellation',
	'terms_4_b' => 'The report is for the named client only. Only you see it, unless you share it. We do not work for the seller or the agent, and we do not send them the report. If a finding needs a structural engineer or another specialist, we say so on the 30-minute call and name the kind of specialist to ask.',
	'terms_4_c' => 'Instructing that person is your decision. The rough cost range is not a quotation and not an offer to do the work. We do not sell or arrange repairs. These terms apply to full reports, to single-defect letters and to re-visit letters. The office is at 3 Ropewalk Yard, Elsmere Quay, and the practice was founded in 2011.',
	'terms_4_h' => 'Who the report is for',
	'terms_i' => 'These terms cover a condition survey instructed from Noki Surveyors. The survey is visual and non-invasive. The report is for the named client only.',
	'terms_l' => 'Terms',
	'terms_t' => 'Terms',
	'thanks_0_b' => 'Thank you. Lucía will reply within one working day. The reply comes from the request desk, by email or by phone, on +00 31 555 0148 or from hello@noki-surveyors.example. Desk hours are Monday to Friday, 08:30–17:30.',
	'thanks_0_c' => 'A request that arrives in those hours is answered within one working day with a fixed price and a visit slot. If you wrote outside desk hours, the working day starts at the next morning the desk is open. You do not need to send the form again while you wait for that reply.',
	'thanks_0_h' => 'Lucía will reply within one working day',
	'thanks_1_b' => 'The reply names the survey that matches the building, the price from the published list, and a visit slot. Flat or small house is EUR 480, a house is EUR 640, a large house is EUR 820, and a small commercial building is EUR 1,150.',
	'thanks_1_c' => 'A single-defect inspection is EUR 290, and a re-visit after repairs is EUR 160. Prices include VAT and travel within 40 km of Elsmere Quay. If the address sits outside that distance, Lucía will say so in the same reply. The price is agreed before anyone comes to site. You pay after the report is sent, within 14 days.',
	'thanks_1_h' => 'What the reply contains',
	'thanks_2_b' => 'On the day, someone needs to let the surveyor in. You are welcome to join for the last 20 minutes, and you do not have to stay for the whole visit. A flat or small house takes about 90 minutes. A house of 90–180 m² takes 2 to 3 hours. A large house takes 3 to 4 hours.',
	'thanks_2_c' => 'A small commercial building takes about 4 hours. A single defect or a re-visit takes about 45 minutes. Site hours are Monday to Saturday, 08:00–17:00, Saturday by arrangement. The full report arrives within five working days, and a short letter within two. A 30-minute call follows. Cancellation is free until 24 hours before the visit.',
	'thanks_2_h' => 'The visit and the report',
	'thanks_3_b' => 'If the address, the building type or the date you need the report by was missing, Lucía will ask for it in the reply. You can also call +00 31 555 0148 or email hello@noki-surveyors.example during desk hours. The surveyors on the visits are Ines Kovač, Tomasz Wren, Adaeze Nwosu and Henrik Saari.',
	'thanks_3_c' => 'Lucía books the slot. We do not sell or arrange repairs, we do not work for the seller or the agent, and a survey is not a valuation. Until the reply arrives, there is nothing further to do on the form.',
	'thanks_3_h' => 'If you need the desk before then',
	'thanks_home' => 'Back to the home page',
	'thanks_i' => 'Lucía will reply within one working day. Your request has reached the desk at 3 Ropewalk Yard, Elsmere Quay.',
	'thanks_l' => 'Thanks',
	'thanks_t' => 'Thanks',
